In the fully force-visible C-II branch, C26 gives at most
    2|B_+|-3 <= 2*pi*D-3
contact bridges.

If S_bridge >= eta D^2, pigeonhole gives a bridge e with
    alpha_e >= eta D^2/(2|B_+|-3)
            >= eta D^2/(2*pi*D-3)
            = (eta/(2*pi)+o(1))D.

C20 identifies alpha_e with the length of the reciprocal-polygon diagonal for e.
Root at the C23 hub.  For the descendant side,
    w_e = exact beta-mass crossing the cut,
    alpha_e <= D w_e <= D.
Therefore the same bridge satisfies
    w_e >= eta D/(2*pi*D-3)
        = eta/(2*pi)+o(1).
The normalized weighted average of crossing diameter directions has magnitude
    alpha_e/(D w_e) >= eta D/(2*pi*D-3).

So bridge-dominant stress forces one genuinely macroscopic reciprocal diagonal and one
cut carrying a nonvanishing fraction of all positive diameter weight.

Exact next bridge target:
exclude fixed-c macroscopic bridge cuts (alpha_e>=cD, w_e>=c).  That would force
S_bridge=o(D^2) and send almost all contact stress into the two-edge-connected branch.
```
